{"title":"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2003 AMC 10B #17</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">2003 AMC 12B #13</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<p>An ice cream cone consists of a sphere of vanilla ice cream and a right circular cone that has the same diameter as the sphere. If the ice cream melts, it will exactly fill the cone. Assume that the melted ice cream occupies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e126f0d41c904d37ba2c332347a24b75d4ac3066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the volume of the frozen ice cream. What is the ratio of the cone's height to its radius? (Note: a cone with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has volume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b99c996a0b4e8d903e88f244d1e592d246099e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2 h / 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"19\" /> and a sphere with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> has volume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/3067d8d93f0faeefd7efa96475f45f95de630225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\pi r^3 / 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"19\" />.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad3f9b4c9a6e16461e11699a801c6ef3742b587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2:1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 3:1 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 4:1 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 16:3 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 6:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"482\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of both the cone and the sphere of ice cream, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the height of the cone. The cone can hold a maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba0770ebce80c7a3ecf73a49db518dfed6b0111f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2h/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"19\" /> melted ice cream. The volume of the frozen ice cream is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfba5ef938691d531f54e356f6dd3b795f1f090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi r^3/3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"19\" /> The volume of the melted ice cream is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b582c9d24f700d771f3612571cf29dbe7503fd25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75 \\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of that, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e755b17489f1bd0e5682e766942c6100be7eeef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^3.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> Since the melted ice cream fills the cone exactly,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1935127b747f9503985ba20a2152ebe193c4714a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\pi r^3&amp;=\\pi r^2h/3\\\\ r&amp;=h/3\\\\ 3&amp;=h/r\\end{align*}\" width=\"106\" height=\"69\" />\n</p><p>Then the ratio of the cone's height to its radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/484694c50807744c1a528927a4409451fe41537f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h:r=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 3:1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"137\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/OQEfY3PweeA\">https://youtu.be/OQEfY3PweeA</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B\">2003 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_